{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T04:34:36.628Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"889f14fd4f565135be7f7e17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1674"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1674: pm list --fields/--compact and pm search print the verbose envelope that GH-1642 removed from the default projection, so --fields costs more than the default"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"GitHub issue #1674 (reported 2026-11-06 against 2026.11.5). Reproduced 2026-11-06 on main 2fd348267 (2026.11.6) against this repository's tracker (3,211 items). pm list --status open --limit 3 (brief) emits 962 B; the same page with --fields id,title emits 1,296 B and with --compact 1,274 B, although both carry smaller rows. pm search \"release workflow\" --limit 3 emits 864 B, with --fields id,title 1,036 B. The --fields and --compact envelopes still carry truncated (repeating has_more), completeness unchecked with two zero unreadable counts, a projection block that echoes the flag just given, filters.limit and filters.fields that repeat applied_limit and the projection, the legacy sort/order echo plus effective_keys as a four-row nested array, a now timestamp, and the 4-line full_item_fields omission_receipt instead of details --full. pm search --fields echoes 13 default-valued filter keys (include_linked false, score_threshold 0, rerank_model, query_expansion_provider, ...) when only --limit was given, and the default search page keeps an items_encoding block whose json_columns and absent lists are empty. Root cause: projectPmBriefListEnvelope (src/sdk/output/list-envelope.ts) only accepts a projection whose mode is brief with the exact BRIEF_LIST_FIELDS, and projectPmBriefSearchEnvelope bails out whenever a projection key exists, so every other read projection falls through to the verbose shape. GH-1642 (pm-gh1642) compacted only the brief page and its AC kept other projections unchanged on purpose, so this is a new defect rather than a recurrence; pm-vhx6 earlier trimmed compact-mode filters through PR #147. Expected: --fields, --compact, --brief and the default list projection, and every pm search projection, share one lean TOON envelope: only explicitly set filters, no projection echo when it equals the flags, completeness only when checked as partial or something was unreadable, the sorting comparator on one line, and the one-line details hint; --full restores the verbose form, and JSON keeps its typed result. Duplicate check: searched fields compact envelope verbose list search projection, GH-1642, GH-1501; nearest owners pm-gh1642 and pm-6pycus are closed and covered the brief page only (create acknowledged the pm-gh1642 overlap with --allow-duplicate for that reason)."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","gh:1674","output","projection","token-efficiency"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-06T04:34:36.628Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T04:34:36.628Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"pm list with --fields or --compact prints the lean TOON envelope of the default brief page: no truncated when it equals has_more, no projection echo, no filters.limit equal to applied_limit and no filters.fields equal to the projection, no now, completeness only when partial, unreadable or unchecked-with-more-pages, sorting as one effective_keys line, and details --full instead of the default full_item_fields omission receipt; pm search with or without --fields prints only explicitly set filters (no default-valued filter keys), no projection echo, no now, no truncated alias and details --full, and an items_encoding block whose json_columns and absent lists are both empty prints only the non-empty list_columns entry; --full, --json, custom or partial omission receipts, unreadable completeness and non-default sorting are unchanged, and the projections stay pure SDK exports that leave their input unchanged; A spec measures the TOON bytes of --fields id,title against the default brief page on the same corpus and asserts the --fields envelope is not larger; Negative control: reverting either projection to brief-only recognition fails the spec"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5t33or"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/reporter","value":"unbraind"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"In any tracker with more than three open items, compare the byte size of pm list --status open --limit 3 with the same command plus --fields id,title or --compact, and pm search <query> --limit 3 with and without --fields id,title"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Every list and search read projection prints the same lean TOON envelope as the default brief page, so --fields never costs more envelope than the default"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"--fields id,title prints 1,296 B against 962 B for the default brief page; search --fields echoes 13 default filter keys, the projection, now and a 4-line omission receipt"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/affected_version","value":"2026.11.5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"list"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-6pycus","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-06T04:34:36.628Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-gh1642","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-06T04:34:36.628Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-vhx6","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-11-06T04:34:36.628Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3f2496d5bdbe936ca320ee9e29ed718985f4b7a92e1f606953a686bb4f27c2f0","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4153a8315fd85e974c1aa1a15490f625382ebd6f919ed16e0db15f3989ac995f"}
