{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T05:08:17.378Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"889f14fd4f565135be7f7e17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1663","claim:pm-gh1674","lineage:pm-gh1663","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1663+pm-gh1674","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1663","claim:pm-gh1674","lineage:pm-gh1663","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"learning_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T05:08:17.378Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/learnings","value":[{"created_at":"2026-11-06T05:08:17.377Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"A presentation compaction keyed to one exact projection shape silently stops applying to every sibling projection. projectPmBriefListEnvelope accepted only mode brief with the exact BRIEF_LIST_FIELDS, so --fields, --compact and a brief page led by another sort field all fell through to the verbose envelope, and the narrower projection cost more than the default. Recognize the projection class (mode plus field list), then bind the echo to the rows: every row must carry exactly the projected keys, otherwise the projection is inconsistent and passes through. Measure each sibling projection against the default on the same corpus in a spec, so the next new projection mode cannot regress unnoticed."}]}],"before_hash":"fa953fa59ffcc5abe1bd7a33ceb4604e4b8fd97824940ae8eca113da3f1e2738","after_hash":"73d3bb6ebf0b79b139d3dd943e6fdc65e6c157a11f55228c72758a4b1e0de7f2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outc