{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-06T05:44:05.279Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"889f14fd4f565135be7f7e17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1663","claim:pm-gh1674","lineage:pm-gh1663","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-gh1663+pm-gh1674","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-gh1663","claim:pm-gh1674","lineage:pm-gh1663","lineage:pm-mpbb","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.319","source":"probe"}},"op":"close","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"Verified on this repository's tracker (byte table in the resolution) and by tests/integration/read-output/projection-envelopes.integration.spec.ts, which runs the built CLI and asserts envelope bytes are no larger than the brief page, plus 77 compact-agent-output specs. Negative control: reverting list-envelope.ts to brief-only recognition fails 4 specs. Full quality:static chain minus mutation passed; focused coverage of the changed modules is 100% on every changed line."},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"pm list --fields/--compact and pm search --fields TOON pages carry no truncated alias, projection echo, now, limit/fields filter echo or four-line omission receipt, and are no larger in envelope than the default brief page; search --fields JSON echoes only set filters"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/claim_principal"},{"op":"remove","path":"/metadata/assignee"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-06T05:44:05.279Z"},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/status","value":"closed"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/closed_at","value":"2026-11-06T05:44:05.251Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/completed_at","value":"2026-11-06T05:44:05.251Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/resolution","value":"projectPmBriefListEnvelope and projectPmBriefSearchEnvelope (src/sdk/output/list-envelope.ts) now recognize any standard row projection (mode brief, compact or fields with a non-empty field list) instead of only the exact brief field list, and they require every row to carry exactly the projected keys, so a producer whose echo disagrees with its rows passes through unchanged. The projection echo is dropped because the row header lists the fields; an empty --fields page keeps it. A filters.fields echo equal to the projection is dropped, and on --fields search pages so are now and a mode_source other than settings. SDK runSearch with a fields projection echoes filters through the same set-only summary as the compact default (buildProjectedSearchFilters), so search --fields JSON no longer carries 13 default-valued keys; --full keeps the verbose echo. Kept by contract: completeness keeps its status line (pm-6pycus), and items_encoding keeps json_columns and absent because decoders detect an encoding block by them. On this tracker, list --fields id,title went from 1,296 B to 887 B, --compact from 1,274 B to 957 B, and search --fields id,title from 1,036 B to 444 B."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/close_reason","value":"Fixed: --fields, --compact and every projected pm search page share the lean TOON envelope of the default brief page"}],"before_hash":"407e008a13defb79dfaa4512a010942971f6aa014a722f0ce9ac182be6248d8d","after_hash":"414c33d155cdf16f4f9bb172564fe05d12b461223995bbff94200c0a92bb73b6","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"completion":{"timestamp":"2026-11-06T05:44:05.251Z","source":"close_time"},"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event